# Every text file keeps LF in the working tree, Windows included. A CRLF checkout would make `dist/` differ from what tsc
# writes (test/dist.test.ts compares them byte for byte) and would break the tests that read SKILL.md frontmatter and the
# templates as they are written. Files git detects as binary — the ones holding control characters on purpose — are untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf
